                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f816672-8e75-42b0-ad74-2bcc47dc337e",
                                "sense_id": "d26a7b28-42c2-3ce0-b733-1b01d20bef81",
                                "text": "It was perhaps the most public example of the “manterruption” – that is, a man interrupting a woman while she’s trying to speak (in this case, on stage, by herself, as an award honoree) and taking over the floor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6510db4f-a40d-497b-befd-c82300769e27",
                                "sense_id": "d26a7b28-42c2-3ce0-b733-1b01d20bef81",
                                "text": "The 18 honorees included some of the Democratic Party’s best-known leaders and boosters: Hillary Clinton, the philanthropist and major Democratic donor George Soros, and Robert F. Kennedy, who was given the recognition posthumously."
                            }
                        ]
